mothershipOS (mship.video): MMAP buffers for the encoder. The encoder is the host's Venus through virtio-media, which
can only share virtio objects (virtio-gpu buffers) as DMABUFs; the client's frames, the format converter's and the
bitstream blocks come from dma-buf heaps. Both queues now use the device's MMAP buffers: each frame is copied in
(any stride to the device's layout), each encoded chunk copied out. ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.encoder_mmap=false
restores the DMABUF queues.

